PATCH 559: selecting any DETAIL level crashes the port -- base-loss in the settings-string builder.

Found by driving the real UI rather than by reading code.  The SETTINGS screen renders correctly (its
CONTROL/DISPLAY/SOUND columns, the LED radio buttons, ACCEPT/CANCEL), and clicking LOW DETAIL at
(237,40) visibly moves the lit LED from HIGH to LOW.  Accepting then SEGVs:

    #0  FUN_0000_6f90 (param_1=35721, param_2=0x0)  build/fist.c:19327
    #1  FUN_0000_6e8d   #2  FUN_0000_6a4a   #3  FUN_0000_e714

`FUN_0000_6f90` (asm 0x6f90-0x7009) builds the settings string.  Six of its ten fields are table
lookups of exactly this shape:

    6f98: 0f b6 1e 45 8b   movzbw 0x8b45,%bx        ; the setting's value
    6f9d: 8a 87 5d 8b      mov    0x8b5d(%bx),%al   ; DS-relative -> byte[DGROUP:0x8b5d + value]
    6fa1: a2 a9 8a         mov    %al,0x8aa9

-- an index into the character table at DGROUP:0x8b5d.  Ghidra emitted the SUM as a host pointer,
`*(undefined1 *)(DAT_2000_4b45 + 0x8b5d)`, so the first lookup dereferences ~0x8b5d and dies.

Two further defects in the same function:

  - the three `>> 1` fields are not lookups but they were mis-widened.  `mov 0x8b47,%ax ; shr $1,%al ;
    add $0x30,%al` loads a WORD and shifts only AL, so the result is `byte[0x8b47] >> 1` + '0';
    Ghidra's `(byte)(word >> 1)` differs whenever bit 8 of the word is set.
  - the tail is `lcall *[0x2b4] ; mov $0x8ab3,%di ; cld ; rep movsb %ds:(%si),%es:(%di)`.  DS and ES are
    both DGROUP here, so the destination is DGROUP:0x8ab3 and the source is DGROUP:si -- Ghidra used
    both as host pointers.

## NOT fixed here

SI arrives as 0.  `FUN_0000_6e8d` BEGINS with the call to this function -- asm 0x6e8d is the call
instruction itself -- so SI is threaded down from 6a4a and above, and the port's arg-less far dispatch
does not carry it.  That is board:0014's carrier class, not this one.  Transcribing the copy as
DGROUP:si is still the faithful reading; the zero is a defect one level up, and with it the copy moves
the wrong bytes instead of faulting.

This patch stops the crash and makes the ten field writes correct.  It does NOT make the detail level
take effect: `byte[TCB+0xd1]` is 4 at the render, outside the 0/1/2 the extender's .DTL loader accepts
(board:0002), so no ramp file loads either way.

board:0007

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -19323,25 +19323,54 @@
   undefined1 *puVar3;
   undefined2 unaff_ES;
   
-  DAT_2000_4aa8 = (char)DAT_2000_4b43 + '0';
-  DAT_2000_4aa9 = *(undefined1 *)(DAT_2000_4b45 + 0x8b5d);
-  DAT_2000_4ab2 = *(undefined1 *)(DAT_2000_4b50 + 0x8b5d);
-  DAT_2000_4aab = *(undefined1 *)(DAT_2000_4b46 + 0x8b5d);
-  DAT_2000_4aac = ((byte)(DAT_2000_4b47 >> 1) & 0x7f) + 0x30;
-  DAT_2000_4aad = ((byte)(DAT_2000_4b49 >> 1) & 0x7f) + 0x30;
-  DAT_2000_4aae = ((byte)(DAT_2000_4b4b >> 1) & 0x7f) + 0x30;
-  DAT_2000_4aaf = *(undefined1 *)(DAT_2000_4b4d + 0x8b5d);
-  DAT_2000_4ab1 = *(undefined1 *)(DAT_2000_4b4e + 0x8b5d);
-  DAT_2000_4ab0 = *(undefined1 *)(DAT_2000_4b4f + 0x8b5d);
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c2b4)))();
-  puVar3 = (undefined1 *)0x8ab3;
-  for (; param_1 != 0; param_1 = param_1 + -1) {
-    puVar2 = puVar3;
-    puVar3 = puVar3 + 1;
-    puVar1 = param_2;
-    param_2 = param_2 + 1;
-    *puVar2 = *puVar1;
+  /* PATCH 559: the SETTINGS-string builder (asm 0x6f90-0x7009), reached from the SETTINGS screen's
+   * accept path (6a4a -> 6e8d -> 6f90).  Every one of its six table lookups is
+   *
